notes = "(!) PSP2UPDAT.PUP is the PS Vita system firmware, downloaded from PlayStation's website, and goes in system/vita3k/ in RetroArch's system directory, as do the preinst and font packages (preinst_fresh.pup / font_fresh.pup are accepted too). The core installs them on first start.|(!) Content: a .vpk or .zip of a game, a game folder's eboot.bin, or the folder itself. The game is installed into system/vita3k/ the first time it is started.|(!) The data and shaders-builtin folders from the release go in system/vita3k/."

description = "Vita3K is an experimental PlayStation Vita emulator. It runs commercial games and homebrew, rendering with Vulkan. This core is a libretro port of it: it installs the firmware and the games from RetroArch's system directory and draws into RetroArch's Vulkan device."
